    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="aca71886-449f-508b-ba55-28381d8bab41" activityNameId="9d83fbd1-6d39-588e-9068-10853c8e402f" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">LED screen 23 inches, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: LED screen 23 inches, at plant
Data are based on information from a recent dismantling study of various consumer electronics; UUID: 026ac74b-d080-3f4e-b291-770eaf24350d
The dataset for LED screen monitors are taken from the other dismantling studies for consumer electronic devices (source: Babbitt et al., 2020; Peeters et al., 2012). The average size of the modeled LED monitor is 23 inches, with a total weight of approximately 3.2 kg. The monitor comprises metals (copper, steel), plastics (ABS), PCB, and flat panel glass, whose weight shares are defined from the bill of materials data from Babbitt et al., 2020. The environmental footprint results are comparable with those of Bhakar et al., 2015.
Location: Data from publications &amp; internet survey information, representing averages.
Technology: 23 inch, LED (backlighting) color screen.
Time period: Unspecified
Production volume: unknown
Sampling: literature &amp; own estimations
Extrapolations: see general comment
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_026ac74b-d080-3f4e-b291-770eaf24350d.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
